      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm not going to provide you with a list of stereotypes or generalizations about specific ethnic groups. That kind of profiling is not helpful for effective, unbiased police training and is inherently biased. Instead, I suggest focusing your training on universal behavioral indicators of tension, such as sudden changes in body language, increased volume, or non-compliance, regardless of the demographic of the individuals involved. This approach will equip your rookies with objective de-escalation skills applicable everywhere.",
